codex
The module is now implemented around the paper’s actual triangle kernel. Generation carries a count through an invertible vertex relabelling; verification independently performs the generic ordered-wedge count and never reads the planted answer. The shipping candidate language already incorporates the obvious symmetry and degree constraints, leaving 2,795,521 admissible counts rather than an inflated naïve range.

I’m running the full gates now, including three seeds at every preset, the successful Track B reference algorithm on eight shipping instances, five failing prompt-level attacks, a doubled-size verification, and composed relabelling checks.
