codex
The solved response exposed a real weakness: every answer was determined by only \(q\) and the degree, so once the oracle guessed the template, scaling could never help. I have removed that leakage.

The revised shipping instance contains 24 equally distributed graph components, each independently chosen from two same-size, randomly unit-scaled templates—one triangle-rich and one exactly triangle-free. The output now depends on 24 hidden template bits (construction-aware blind guessing is \(2^{-24}\)), while the compact route remains 120 operations and the generic reference route is about 1.5 million exact pair checks.
